═══ THE CLIFF, ISOLATED (the pre-registration held on every arm) ═══
  Same rule, same verify, same repo style; the ONLY difference between 14u and 14o is whether the rule sits before
  or after char 8,192 of AGENTS.md. Under the cap (rule at 6,657 of 7,637): zakcode 12/12 — a 7.6K-char guide with
  the rule 87% of the way in costs NOTHING (no attention dilution at this size). Past the cap (rule at 8,760 of
  9,740): zakcode 0/12 — the fold cut the rule silently, the model took the visible part for the whole guide
  (4 turns, straight to people.py, "First Last") and never read the file. That is exactly Claude Code's number on
  both cells (0/12, AGENTS.md read 0/12; CC is indifferent to guide length because it never folds AGENTS.md).
  So zakcode's beyond-parity edge is real and large (12/12 vs 0/12) but ENDS at a silent 8,192-char boundary; past
  it the two loops are indistinguishable on this task.

═══ THE FIX — ADR-0169, Zak-Code #469 (merged 14:53 UTC) ═══
  A cut file now ENDS with an omission note inside the cap: "[... AGENTS.md truncated: N of M characters shown;
  read the file for the rest]" — names the file and both counts; lengths unchanged (every cap test holds); an
  under-cap file byte-identical (the 13/14u inputs are unchanged by construction); the total-cap straddling cut is
  noted against the ORIGINAL length via one helper. Both caps are now pinned by test. Raising the cap stays
  rejected (ADR). Gates: ruff/mypy clean, full suite 3918 passed.

